    "title": "BIP54: correct the block interval figure in footnote 4",
    "user": {
      "login": "treib-holdings",
      "id": 265589794,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOD9SUIg",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265589794?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/treib-holdings",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/treib-holdings/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Footnote 4 says a two-hour grace period instead of ten minutes \"only reduces the expected block interval time under attack by ~2.2 seconds\", and points to the [grace period summary post](https://delvingbitcoin.org/t/great-consensus-cleanup-revival/710/66). That post gives one block every 599.9997 seconds with a ten-minute grace and 596.7211 seconds with two hours, from [Pieter Wuille's simulation](https://delvingbitcoin.org/t/timewarp-attack-600-second-grace-period/1326/32). The difference is 3.28 seconds. The post's ~0.1% and ~0.65% block rate figures also come to about 3.3 seconds.\n\nI got the same result independently. A simulation of the attack using Bitcoin Core's retarget arithmetic gives 599.71 and 596.43 seconds (3.27 s), and the closed form (7200 - 600) / 2016 gives 3.27 s.\n\nThis changes ~2.2 to ~3.3. The rationale is unaffected: the two-hour grace still only trivially worsens the block rate under attack.\n",
